def Set.IsAPOfLengthWith (s : Set α) (l : ℕ∞) (a d : α) : Prop :=
  ENat.card s = l ∧ s = {a + n • d | (n : ℕ) (_ : n < l)}

def Set.IsAPOfLength (s : Set α) (l : ℕ∞) : Prop := ∃ a d, s.IsAPOfLengthWith l a d

An arithmetic progression of length l is a set {a, a+d, …, a+(l-1)d} with cardinality l. A monochromatic AP is one whose elements all receive the same color (see ContainsMonoAPofLength).

def monoAP_guarantee_set (r k : ℕ) : Set ℕ :=
  { N | ∀ coloring : Finset.Icc 1 N → Fin r, ContainsMonoAPofLength coloring k }

The guarantee set collects the N for which every r-coloring of {1,…,N} contains a monochromatic k-AP. Its nonemptiness (van der Waerden's theorem) is recorded as the axiom W_is_nonempty, so W k = sInf (monoAP_guarantee_set 2 k) is well-defined.

def QuotientDiverges : Prop :=
  Tendsto (fun k => (W (k + 1) : ℝ) / (W k : ℝ)) atTop atTop

def DifferenceDiverges : Prop :=
  Tendsto (fun k => ((W (k + 1) : ℤ) - (W k : ℤ))) atTop atTop

def ExponentialDiverges : Prop :=
  Tendsto (fun k => (W k : ℝ) / 2 ^ k) atTop atTop
